.Dd October 6, 2026
.Dt DISPLAY-SESSION-RESTORE 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm display-session-restore
.Nd restore the saved display mode
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
replays the display mode saved in
.Pa ~/.cache/display-mode .
Any window manager can run it at session start.
.Cm laptop
runs
.Xr display-laptop-only 1
.Fl Fl quiet .
.Cm mirror
runs
.Xr display-mirror-toggle 1
.Fl Fl on Fl Fl quiet .
.Cm extend:left ,
.Cm extend:right ,
and
.Cm extend:above
run
.Xr display-extend 1
with the matching position and
.Fl Fl quiet .
.Pp
An empty mode, the mode
.Cm layout ,
or an unknown mode runs
.Pa ~/.screenlayout/my-monitors.sh
when that file is executable, records
.Cm layout ,
and pauses briefly before returning.
.Pp
The program returns when the helper finishes, so the caller can
do its own aftercare.
.Pp
The shared RandR helpers are
.Pa @PREFIX@/libexec/bhotkeys/display-randr-common.subr .
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Nm
exits 0 when the saved mode is applied or when there is no layout
script to run.
A failing helper exits with that helper's status.
A bad argument exits 2.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr bhotkeys 1 ,
.Xr display-extend 1 ,
.Xr display-laptop-only 1 ,
.Xr display-mirror-toggle 1 ,
.Xr xrandr 1
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Devin Teske Aq Mt dteske@FreeBSD.org
